{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>A woman of beautiful form.</b> It mentioned 'woman' in a construct construction, and our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: even a married woman. And Scripture tells you that she is permitted to be taken by way of conversion and kiddushin, for there is no prohibition of marriage-bond applying to a Canaanite, even though she converts only out of fear." "<b>And you shall bring her into your house.</b> And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: this teaches that he must not force himself upon her in battle. And the intention is that he brings her into a private place and lies with her in a first intercourse, and does not force himself upon her in battle at all, in the manner of what is written (Deuteronomy 23:15): ״ולא יראה בך ערות דבר״. And the reason she was permitted to him in a first intercourse is to appease his inclination, for the Torah spoke only against the evil inclination — since he desired her, if it were impossible for him through permitted means he would do so through forbidden means. Hence it says: והבאתה אל תוך ביתך — this is the first intercourse; and if he wishes to lie with her a second time, וגלחה את ראשה ועשתה והסירה ובכתה — and afterward תבא אליה ובעלתה in a second intercourse. And from this Tamar was permitted to Amnon, for Maacah her mother conceived her from a first intercourse and she was a daughter of a Cuthean woman, and this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory said: Tamar was a daughter of a woman of beautiful form, as she said to Amnon (II Samuel 13:13–14): ״דבר נא אל המלך כי לא ימנעני ממך״ — for if David had lain with Maacah only after conversion, then she was certainly his full sister of Amnon, and how could she say כי לא ימנעני ממך? Rather, she was certainly conceived from a first intercourse, that is, before conversion, and she is thus a daughter of a Cuthean woman, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said: the child of your son who comes from a Cuthean woman is not called your son but her son."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:52.484514673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}